06:55:24,480 --> 06:55:25,060
What is that?

4727
06:55:26,574 --> 06:55:27,716
Oh my goodness.

4728
06:55:28,240 --> 06:55:31,556
This is not my drawing. This is the source for the drawing.

4729
06:55:32,560 --> 06:55:36,400
But this is a seven layers model.

4730
06:55:37,262 --> 06:55:41,764
All right, It looks like a building to me, or at least the skeleton of a building.

4731
06:55:42,414 --> 06:55:48,324
But what is that for? So the OSI model is just a framework, a collection of standards

4732
06:55:49,390 --> 06:55:58,148
that breaks down how data travels across a network from the user using an application, let's say Chrome, for example,

4733
06:55:58,880 --> 06:56:00,240
until it reaches.

4734
06:56:00,430 --> 06:56:05,060
So if this is on this side, until it gets to the server on the other side.

4735
06:56:05,360 --> 06:56:18,880
So from the user that from the application, the client application, through the network, through the LAN and one until it gets to the other side and it is received and comprehended by the receiver.

4736
06:56:19,054 --> 06:56:20,804
That's what the OSI layer defines.

4737
06:56:21,838 --> 06:56:25,988
So the different layers will define things like what are the standards for cabling.

4738
06:56:26,574 --> 06:56:30,596
So that would be the first layer. The physical layer will identify that.

4739
06:56:31,246 --> 06:56:41,924
And what type of cables we can use, and what type of signals, and what is the standards for the optical signals, and what's the standard for the electrical signals,

4740
06:56:42,160 --> 06:56:50,160
and what's the length of the cable, and how many wires should we use, and what type of wires should we use, what type of connectors we should use.

4741
06:56:50,350 --> 06:56:52,388
All of that is defined as standards,

4742
06:56:53,166 --> 06:57:01,508
such that if we bring one connector from China and one cable from Brazil, and then we get the copper wires

4743
06:57:02,670 --> 06:57:13,120
from the US and we get the cramping tools from Japan, or the tools that we use to make the cable, all of them are going to work without any issues.

4744
06:57:13,280 --> 06:57:22,468
And when we connect that to hardware switches or routers that are coming from Taiwan, for example, and they are coming from Vietnam,

4745
06:57:22,734 --> 06:57:32,932
then all of that is going to work without any issues. Why? Because everyone is following the standard, and that is why it ends up working like charm without any issues.

4746
06:57:33,678 --> 06:57:40,036
Alright, for the switches, then the second layer, the data link layer, will specify

4747
06:57:40,974 --> 06:57:44,400
any required information and standards about the switches.

4748
06:57:44,480 --> 06:57:54,240
like the protocols: the protocols for the LAN, the protocols for wide area network, the protocols for data center, as far as switching is concerned,

4749
06:57:54,400 --> 06:57:56,080
and NIC cards are concerned.

4750
06:57:56,206 --> 06:57:59,076
All of that is defined here. So if you bring in

4751
