A laptop or a server that has a NIC card, a network interface card that you bought from China.

4752
06:58:05,872 --> 06:58:07,812
The server is from Korea.

4753
06:58:08,192 --> 06:58:17,700
And then you bring in the cable from Taiwan and you connect all of these and you connect it to the switch from the US, all of that is going to work without any problems.

4754
06:58:18,286 --> 06:58:21,392
This is going to be data link layer, as it is called.

4755
06:58:21,518 --> 06:58:24,644
So it defines the standards for switching and related.

4756
06:58:25,518 --> 06:58:34,672
Then we have layer three. And please note that there are seven layers, and that's why when we say layer one, layer two, layer three, layer four, layer seven, you know what we are talking about.

4757
06:58:34,862 --> 06:58:43,300
So when we say that a device functions at layer seven, then you should understand that it understands all the application headers and stuff like that.

4758
06:58:44,622 --> 06:58:51,044
The most important ones that always are relevant are layer three, layer four, and layer seven.

4759
06:58:51,232 --> 06:58:54,752
You need to know these like the back of your hand. What do they do?

4760
06:58:54,912 --> 06:58:55,780
What's their function?

4761
06:58:57,710 --> 06:59:08,192
Layer three is about the network. So it defines the standards for the routers, the interfaces, the routing protocols, the ping ICMP, IPsec,

4762
06:59:08,430 --> 06:59:11,632
we'll talk about it later on for scrambling the data.

4763
06:59:11,872 --> 06:59:17,028
IP, OSPF, a lot of things will function at this layer

4764
06:59:17,792 --> 06:59:19,844
that have to do with routing.

4765
06:59:20,942 --> 06:59:24,512
Then we get into the fourth one, the transport.

4766
06:59:24,752 --> 06:59:35,152
So this is the bus that will take the data from one side and will establish a connection with the other side, and then we'll send the data down to get there.

4767
06:59:35,470 --> 06:59:40,132
So that's the transport, the connection between the two sides that needs to be done.

4768
06:59:40,654 --> 06:59:46,948
And this will define a lot of things that we are going to discuss: TCP, UDP, SSL, TLS. We are going to talk about all of these.

4769
06:59:47,726 --> 06:59:52,912
Then we have session, which is controlling the communication.

4770
06:59:53,134 --> 06:59:57,712
You are opening your browser and talking to the website or the

4771
06:59:58,958 --> 07:00:01,392
e-commerce, Amazon.com, for example.

4772
07:00:01,614 --> 07:00:05,988
So that session between your application and the other side, who is managing that?

4773
07:00:06,192 --> 07:00:07,588
That will be the session layer.

4774
07:00:08,334 --> 07:00:09,700
In the two sides, by the way.

4775
07:00:10,286 --> 07:00:11,872
And then we have the presentation.

4776
07:00:11,952 --> 07:00:21,152
So this one defines the session information and how the session should be between the two sides, how to open the sessions, how to close the sessions,

4777
07:00:21,312 --> 07:00:23,236
what are the messages exchanged for that.

4778
07:00:23,534 --> 07:00:24,964
This is all at the session layer.

4779
07:00:26,286 --> 07:00:36,164
And then we have the presentation that decides how the data should look like and if there is any scrambling for security, which is called encryption. We're going to cover that later on.

4780
07:00:37,038 --> 07:00:39,952
If it is required, then this layer will take care of that.

4781
07:00:40,078 --> 07:00:48,708
And then we have the application layer that defines if you are working with DNS, HTTP for browsers or HTTPS and all that stuff.

4782
07:00:49,538 --> 07:01:00,272
All right, Each one of these layers define the standards and how the protocols or the frames or the format of the data should be at every single layer.

4783
07:01:00,352 --> 07:01:10,148
How to establish a session, how to establish a connection between the two sides, how the network should look like, and how every one of these headers related to these

4784
07:01:10,670 --> 07:01:17,572
services or functions will be identified in the packet, and it has to be standard across everything.

4785
07:01:17,838 --> 07:01:19,072
And that is how

4786
07:01:19,918 --> 07:01:23,872
the end points they will be able to communicate without any problem.

4787
07:01:24,078 --> 07:01:25,860
Okay, so the framework

4788
07:01:26,830 --> 07:01:35,792
in seven understandable steps, each one doing a specific job that's for a successful communication from one end device, let's say my laptop,

4789
07:01:35,952 --> 07:01:37,412
with a server in a data center.

4790
07:01:39,246 --> 07:01:42,832
The packet as it starts, it will start at the user.

4791
07:01:43,150 --> 07:01:52,432
So the user will open the browser, let's say, for example, it doesn't have to be a browser, it could be a client, Uber, for example, Uber application or Google Maps,

4792
07:01:52,592 --> 07:01:54,372
and going to the Google server.

4793
07:01:56,142 --> 07:02:03,076
So the user will start whatever he is doing here or she's doing here, and that will be the payload, the data itself.

4794
07:02:04,110 --> 07:02:06,916
So the stack of TCP,

4795
07:02:07,888 --> 07:02:14,724
or the stack of services that have to do with networks inside your laptop, or her laptop, or his laptop,

4796
07:02:15,568 --> 07:02:24,368
the application layer is going to start getting that data and then deciding on what headers are going to be added and how to facilitate

4797
07:02:24,528 --> 07:02:25,956
its access to the network.

4798
07:02:27,086 --> 07:02:32,768
The presentation layer will look. Do we need any scrambling? Do we need to add any headers that relates to that?

4799
07:02:32,848 --> 07:02:36,964
And then the session layer will decide how the session would be and will manage the session.

4800
07:02:37,646 --> 07:02:43,968
So these three are going to prepare the data the right way so it will be sent to the other side.

4801
07:02:44,128 --> 07:02:49,188
If it needs scrambling, if it doesn't need scrambling, how it should look like, if there are any headers to be added, and so on.

4802
07:02:50,862 --> 07:02:55,844
Then it gets down to the function that does the transport layer.

4803
07:02:56,128 --> 07:02:59,396
Everything we are talking about right now is inside the laptop.

